# Conventional Commits

Only create commits when the user **explicitly** asks in the current message — see `.cursor/rules/git-workflow.mdc`. When they do, **always** use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/).

## Format

```text
<type>(<scope>): <description>

[optional body]

[optional footer(s)]
```

- **type** and **description** are required.
- **scope** is recommended for this monorepo.
- **description**: imperative mood, lowercase, no period at end, max ~72 chars on first line.
- **body**: wrap at ~72 chars; explain *why*, not only *what*.
- **footer**: `BREAKING CHANGE: ...` or `Refs DEV-123` when relevant.

## Types

| Type | Use when |
|---|---|
| `feat` | New user-facing capability |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `style` | Formatting, no logic change |
| `refactor` | Code change, no feat/fix |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |
| `test` | Tests only |
| `build` | Build system, dependencies |
| `ci` | CI/CD, GitHub Actions |
| `chore` | Maintenance, tooling, misc |
| `revert` | Reverts a prior commit |

## Scopes (this repo)

`frontend` · `backend` · `docs` · `db` · `infra` · `docker` · `deps`

Omit scope only for repo-wide changes (e.g. root README).

## Examples

```text
feat(backend): add POST /api/v1/auth/login with Identity JWT

fix(frontend): redirect unauthenticated users to /login on app host

docs: document Identity completo and Resend noreply strategy

ci: run EF migrations on Supabase direct connection in deploy workflow

chore(deps): bump @nuxt/eslint to 0.5.0
```

## Rules

- Never use vague messages: `update`, `fix stuff`, `wip`, `changes`.
- One logical change per commit when possible.
- Do **not** commit secrets (`.env`, API keys, connection strings).
- Only commit when the user explicitly asks (unless their rules say otherwise).
- Full reference: `docs/CONVENTIONAL_COMMITS.md`
